<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Alpinvest posts higher 1996 net profit.</title>
<headline>Dutch Alpinvest posts higher 1996 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				  88.0  vs  71.0</p>
<p>Total dividend and interest income  30.9  vs  35.0</p>
<p>    Total operational costs		 11.3  vs   9.8</p>
<p>    Profits on stakeholdings sold	 68.4  vs  45.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Venture capital company Alpinvest Holding NV will seek a listing on the Amsterdam Stock Exchange later this year. The company is presently owned by the Dutch state and various institutional investors. ABN AMRO is the largest stakeholder with an interest of 48.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
